error: rsjs boundary: `rsjs::server_attr(...)` cannot capture reactive signal `selected`

       Why:
         Server-only attributes emit static SSR values. Client hydration does not attach reactive updates to that attribute.

       Use one of:
         - Use a normal dynamic attribute for values that should update on the client.
         - If the value is intentionally static, pass plain server data through `rsjs::server_attr(...)`.

       Tracked feature:
         server_boundary.server_attr_signal_capture
